{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they do not</b> — the meaning is: when they wail at night upon their beds and say, 'Woe to them for the evil coming upon them,' they do not cry out to Him, as the sick man cries out to the physician." "<b>And the meaning of they assemble for grain and new wine</b> — that they gather by day to eat and drink, like 'were broken down from the granaries' [2 Kings 10:27 נהרסו ממגורות]." "<b>They turn away from Me</b> — they speak treason against Me. And behold, at night they do not cry out to Him, and by day they rebel to speak lies."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:32.671770531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}